Package: bayome
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Occurrence-Abundance Microbiome Estimation
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Joaquín", "Martínez-Minaya",
           email = "jmartinezminaya@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayesian models for microbiome association studies. The
    occurrence (presence/absence) and the abundance of each feature are
    modelled together, the abundance effects are linked to the occurrence
    effects, and information is shared across features, which stabilises
    the estimates of features with few observations. Models are fitted with
    the integrated nested Laplace approximation ('R-INLA'). The interface is
    compatible with 'MaAsLin3' (Nickols et al. 2026
    <doi:10.1038/s41592-025-02923-9>): the same arguments, the same
    'lme4'-style formulas and the same output columns.
